  "reason": "Evidence: The best-performing configuration so far is config_045 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc. All top-performing configs use weighted fusion, but we have no evidence on how concat fusion performs in this strong regime—concat was only tested with weaker scgpt encoders. Question: config_007 changes exactly one variable from config_045 (fusion: weighted → concat), cleanly isolating the effect of fusion strategy when the RNA encoder and image encoder are both strong. Why this is the best next experiment: It is the most informative single-variable test available—either it confirms weighted fusion is essential (narrowing the design space) or shows concat is competitive (broadening it). Under a limited budget, this directly informs whether fusion choice is a critical design axis or a minor one, and it avoids simultaneously changing multiple variables as would happen with, e.g., testing a new image encoder and a new fusion at once."
